sections:
  - title: "Forming an LLC in New York: what to expect"
    body:
      - "Forming an LLC in New York takes a few more steps than in most states. After the Articles of Organization are filed with the Department of State, New York law requires a new LLC to publish a notice in two newspapers, once a week for six weeks, within 120 days of formation, and then file a Certificate of Publication. An LLC that skips this step can have its authority to do business suspended. Publication costs vary widely by county."
      - "Once you're set up, you'll need an EIN, a business bank account and, if you sell taxable goods or services, a sales tax Certificate of Authority. Corporations and LLCs also file a biennial statement with the state every two years."
