faq:
  - q: "Should I form an LLC or a corporation?"
    a: "It depends on how you want to be taxed, how many owners you have and your plans to grow. Many small businesses start as an LLC because it's simple to run, and an S corporation election can reduce self-employment tax once profits grow. We'll walk through the numbers with you."
  - q: "What is the New York LLC publication requirement?"
    a: "Within 120 days of forming, a New York LLC must publish a notice of its formation in two newspapers, once a week for six consecutive weeks, then file a Certificate of Publication with the Department of State. Skipping it can suspend the LLC's authority to do business in New York."
  - q: "How do I get an EIN?"
    a: "An EIN is issued by the IRS free of charge. We apply for it as part of setting up your business, so you can open a bank account and hire employees."
